      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is 5 times that. It risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity (QT prolongation). Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg entered as 1000 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order is clinically intended.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. Usual adult dosing is 25\u2013200 mg once daily, depending on the indication.\n- If a prescriber confirms a corrected dose, such as 100 mg by mouth once daily, they or another clinician can ask me to enter it. I can enter it then.\n- If the dose really is 1000 mg, the order needs direct prescriber review and pharmacy involvement before anything is entered."
      }
     ],
