       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the issues, because you've said you're not a clinician or prescriber. The dose is also 5 times the maximum recommended daily dose, so I can't treat it as a reasonable order. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nWhat I'd suggest:\n- **Contact the prescriber.** If someone on the medicine service wrote this order, ask them to check the dose. It may be a typo for 100 mg.\n- **Involve pharmacy.** If the dose is truly intended, for example in an overdose or toxicology setting, a prescriber should enter it directly and pharmacy should review it.\n- **Let a clinician ask me.** Once a prescriber confirms a safe dose, they can ask me to enter it. I'm happy to do that right away.\n\nI'm sorry I can't do more on this one."
